(:spec :id conductorConfig :v 1 :date "2026-10-30" :file "<conductor store>/ladder.asn" :reader "asl/tools/coord/conductor.asl pfCfg rungCap" :check "asl/tools/coord/conductor.asl pfErrors (tested in conductorTest testProviderFail)"
  :doc "per-store escalation settings of the conductor, one row per line; the store is the --store directory of the conductor (~/.asl/run/conductor on the node). A missing file or row means the documented default, a (:providerFail) row that pfErrors rejects is ignored whole and the defaults apply"
  :rung "(:rung :tier paid|strong :perDay N): caps the units that enter that rung per UTC day; no row is no cap; the lead rung is never capped but is open only while the lead heartbeat <store>/leadOnline.asn is younger than 120 s (ESC-LEAD-HOOK)"
  :providerFail "(:providerFail :backoffS S :maxInRow N :patterns (\"word\" ...)) with :patterns last, words lowercase-compared as substrings of the failed write's signature and without parentheses. A write that fails with a matching signature and no commit past its base (not stale, not vacuous) is requeued after :backoffS seconds with its fail count, signature and lane unchanged, one (:providerFail :unit :route :backoffS :n :at) row is journalled and the newest (:pw :unit :n :until) row of <store>/providerWait.asn holds the wait; the :maxInRow+1th consecutive provider failure is an ordinary failure (counted, ladder hop), any other outcome resets the run"
  :ranges "backoffS 1..3600 (default 60, adopted), maxInRow 1..100 (default 6, adopted), patterns non-empty (default err_vendor err_no_upstream \"bad gateway\" \"service unavailable\" overloaded \" 502\" \" 503\" \" 504\" \" 429\" breaker, adopted); unknown keys and out-of-range values are errors"
  :writers "(:writers :minFreeMb N :warmFirst true|false :jobserver \"DIR\" :meminfo \"PATH\") (COND-ADMIT-TOKENS): a ready unit starts its writer only while the node has a free jobserver token (tokenCount minus heldCount) and MemAvailable >= :minFreeMb; with :warmFirst (default true) the first writer after each conductor start goes alone and the rest wait until its session journal shows a served model turn, its unit left writing, or 900 s passed, recorded in <store>/warm.asn. No row, or a row with an unknown key or :minFreeMb outside 0..1000000, means no gate (checked by wrErrors, tested in conductorTest testAdmitGate). :jobserver and :meminfo default to the node's own ~/.asl/run/jobserver and /proc/meminfo and exist for tests"
  :writersRanges "minFreeMb 0..1000000 (default 2000, adopted); warmFirst default true (adopted); the node ships the row in <store>/ladder.asn, the code default without a row is no gate"
  :stall "(:stall :stalledMin M :sameOp N :emptyReplies K :escalateAfter E :everyS S) (COND-STALL-AUTO), read by asl/tools/coord/stall.asl cfgOf and checked by cfgErrors (tested in stallTest): at most every :everyS seconds each writing unit gets a verdict from its newest session journal under <worktree>/.asl/run/agentLoop and the newest file write outside .git .asl node_modules out: dead (the run record's pid is gone), looping (the last :sameOp replies are identical, or the last :emptyReplies are empty), stalled (no served turn and no file write for :stalledMin minutes), else ok. A non-ok unit gets one (:stall :unit :class :op :escalate :at) row in <store>/stalls.asn, its tree killed through the run record, and is requeued with the note (:stall :class C :n N :op \"...\") in its next task text; the :escalateAfter-th stall of one unit sends it to the strong lane. No row, or a row cfgErrors rejects, means no sweep"
  :stallRanges "stalledMin 1..1440 (default 20, adopted), sameOp 3..1000 (default 10, adopted), emptyReplies 1..100 (default 4, adopted), escalateAfter 1..20 (default 2, adopted), everyS 5..3600 (default 60, adopted). Calibrated on 662 node2 sessions with a served turn (journals under ~/wt/worktrees/asex-*/.asl/run/agentLoop, 2026-10-30): wall per served turn p50 48 s, p90 165 s, p99 396 s, max 534 s, so 20 min is 2.2x the slowest session average; over all 708 journals the longest run of one identical reply was 0 in 46, 1 in 278, 2 to 5 in 301, 6 to 9 in 49 and 10 or more in 34 (4 of them 42 to 417), so sameOp 10 cuts 34 sessions; no empty-reply run was matched in 709 journals by awk on the reply row, so emptyReplies 4 is unmeasured"
  :conductor "(:conductor :staleWakeMax N) (COND-REBASE-WAKE-LOOP): how many failed wakes a unit blocked :await rebase gets before it parks behind its (:lead :unit :needs rebase) row. A parked unit wakes again only when its own branch sh/ID in the deployed repo changes head (someone rebased it) or the lead row is cleared; the deployed main moving alone never wakes it. Read by staleWakeMax, checked by cdErrors (tested in conductorTest testStaleWakeMax); a row cdErrors rejects means the default"
  :conductorRanges "staleWakeMax 1..100 (default 1, adopted); unknown keys and out-of-range values are errors"
  :gate "(:gate :checkTimeoutS N) (GATE-CHECK-TIMEOUT): the seconds the asl check before a unit gate may run, default 900 (adopted; the old fixed 300 s killed leonServe.asl checks 7 times on a loaded node2). A check that passes the bound is the signature gateTimeout and the unit stays in gating, journaled as (:stop :unit :kind gateTimeout :n N) without a fail count; the fourth in a row fails the gate. Read by gateCheckS, checked by gateErrors (tested in conductorWireTest testGateCheckTimeout)"
  :gateRanges "checkTimeoutS 30..7200 (default 900, adopted); unknown keys and out-of-range values are errors, the default is used"
  :wake "(:wake :await NAME :readyBelow N) (INTAKE-PARKED-WAKE), any number of rows: units parked in awaitReview on NAME (an intake class or lane that no allowance refresh ever names) wake while a writer slot is free (tokens minus in-flight) and fewer than N units are ready, one per slot, in file order. No row means nothing wakes this way. Read by freeWake!, checked by wakeErrors (tested in conductorTest testFreeWake); a row wakeErrors rejects is ignored"
  :wakeRanges "readyBelow 1..1000; :await non-empty; unknown keys are errors"
  :backpressure "(:backpressure :maxMerging N) (MERGE-TRAIN-THROUGHPUT), read by asl/tools/coord/conductor.asl bpMaxOf and checked by bpErrors (tested in mergeThroughputTest): no ready unit starts its writer while more than N units are in merging, launched or waiting their turn; gating, review and merge stages are not held; a row bpErrors rejects holds nothing and is reported as a config problem by startupProblemsIn (conductor check, refused at run), like a lane problem; status carries (:bpHeld :merging N :max M) while writers are held and the journal one (:bpHeld) row and one (:bpReleased) row per transition"
  :backpressureRanges "maxMerging 0..10000; no row (default) holds nothing; unknown keys are errors"
  :train "(:train :jobs N) (MERGE-TRAIN-THROUGHPUT), read by asl/tools/coord/conductor.asl trainArgv and checked by trainErrors (tested in mergeThroughputTest): the merge stage passes -j N to asl train; a row trainErrors rejects passes no -j and is reported as a config problem by startupProblemsIn (conductor check, refused at run), like a lane problem"
  :trainRanges "jobs 1..64; no row (default) passes no -j, so the train keeps its own default of 2; unknown keys are errors"
  :mergeRed "(:mergeRed :fixRounds N) (MERGE-RED-TO-WRITER), read by asl/tools/coord/conductor.asl mergeRedRounds and checked by mergeRedErrors (tested in mergeRedFixTest): a merge train red whose every fresh red the train attributes to this unit's branch alone (receipt present, no kill, no failed train, no commit error, nothing preexisting, no assert loss, no combination, interaction or bisection) sends the unit back to its writer on the same branch sh/UNIT instead of retrying the train: one (:mergeRed :action fixRound :round K :of N) journal row, a move merging -> ready at stage mergeRed with signature mergeRedFix K/N: SIG, and the addendum (:mergeRed :round K :of N :branch B :red ((:suite P :exit E :asserts A :err TEXT) ...) :more M :must TEXT) appended to the next brief; the unit then passes gating and review again. After N rounds since its last operator requeue, or at once when the red is the one the last round was sent for (same key), the unit escalates to blocked with one (:mergeRed :action escalate :why exhausted|unchanged) row; status lists units in a round under (:mergeRedFix (\"ID K/N\" ...)). A row mergeRedErrors rejects is 0 and is reported as a config problem by startupProblemsIn, like a lane problem"
  :mergeRedRanges "fixRounds 0..10; no row (default) is 0, the merge failure path before the row existed (retry, maxSame escalates); unknown keys are errors; addendum bounds adopted: 4 suites, 600 bytes of error text each"
  :flow "(:flow :order (merge gate review fix new) :newWhen idle|always) (FLOW-DRAIN), read by asl/tools/coord/conductor.asl flowStep! and checked by flowErrors (tested in flowDrainTest): the tick steps the units class by class in :order, each class with the slots the classes before it left (pace tokens minus units in flight, counted again per class): merge (merging), gate (gating), review (awaitReview, reviewing), fix (ready or writing with a branch already written or a merge-red fix round), new (no branch yet); with :newWhen idle no new unit is admitted while a class before new has runnable work without a slot (a merging unit waiting its train turn, a gating unit not launched, an unparked awaitReview unit, a ready fix round with lane room and no provider backoff), shown in status and <store>/flowHeld.asn as (:flowHeld :stage new :by ((:stage S :ids (...)))) and journalled once per hold as (:flowHeld) and (:flowReleased); :backpressure :maxMerging N is the special case that holds every ready unit while more than N units are merging and keeps working beside this row"
  :flowRanges ":order a permutation of merge gate review fix new (default that order), :newWhen idle or always (default always); no row (default) steps the units in store order with one capacity as before; unknown keys and other values are errors reported by startupProblemsIn"
  :dwell "(:dwell :STATE S ...) (FLOW-DRAIN), read by asl/tools/coord/conductor.asl dwellNote! and checked by dwellErrors (tested in flowDrainTest): STATE is any of queued ready writing gating awaitReview reviewing merging blocked failed and S the seconds a unit may stay there; a unit past its bound gets one (:dwell :unit :st :since :ageS :boundS :reason :at) journal row per stay in that state (its :since, remembered in <store>/dwell/ID.asn). Status prints per state one (:state :st S :n N :oldest ID :ageS A :reason R) row whatever the row says; a unit row written before :since existed has age -1 until its next move"
  :dwellRanges "each bound 1..10000000 seconds; at least one state; no row (default) journals nothing; unknown states and other values are errors reported by startupProblemsIn"
  :origin "COND-PROVIDER-FAIL-NO-HOP: 73 of 313 Leon sessions in 12 h on node2 ended ERR_VENDOR (all-breaker, rate limit) and each climbed the ladder as a writer failure")
